            <ArticleTitle>Troubleshooting in transradial intervention.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A54-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The transradial approach to coronary intervention has been shown to have a lower rate of complication than transfemoral access. Nevertheless complications can still occur and in this article we focus on how to avoid and manage these problems.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
